Freifunk Jena WireGuard Onboarder
=================================

Configure /etc/freifunk-jena-wireguard-onboarder/config.ini before enabling
the service. You need two WireGuard interfaces:

- [wireguard.innercity] — LibreMesh node IP (client-supplied AllowedIPs)
- [wireguard.wan] — WAN uplink; server allocates AllowedIPs from address_pool

Align interface names, config paths, CIDRs, and reserved addresses with your
VPN before starting.

There is no application authentication. Bind to a trusted network or restrict
the port with a firewall.

Enable and start:

  systemctl enable --now freifunk-jena-wireguard-onboarder.service

Managed peer state is stored in
/var/lib/freifunk-jena-wireguard-onboarder/state.json. Only peers recorded
there are expired by the watchdog (removed from both tunnel confs).

LibreMesh nodes should POST to /register on boot and whenever their node IP
changes. The JSON response includes the allocated WAN address.
